# TP Reviews Engine - paths Prettier must not touch.
#
# The governing principle is FMT-01: reformatting a captured page changes
# whitespace-sensitive extraction behaviour, and reformatting a generated file
# makes a comparison run against something its generator did not produce.

# --- FMT-01. The two normative exclusions. ---

# Captured markup. Reformatting changes what the parser sees.
fixtures/**/page.html

# Golden extraction output, generated by the engine and byte-compared.
fixtures/**/expected.json

# The rest of the corpus is data on the same terms.
fixtures/**/meta.json
fixtures/**/*.csv

# --- Baselined documents ---
#
# DEVIATION FROM IMPL PLAN 20.1, WHICH LISTS docs/** AS FORMATTED.
#
# These four document sets were authored, reviewed, and baselined before this
# repository existed. Their bytes are the approval record. Reformatting 70
# approved files inside a week-1 formatting commit changes approved artifacts
# without approval, and 20.1's stated reason - "documentation diffs stay
# readable" - is about documents this project writes going forward, not about
# a 350,000-word governing corpus that arrived complete.
#
# The single-file documents are additionally generated by scripts/build-*.sh
# from these parts. Formatting either side alone makes the generated file stop
# matching its generator, which is precisely the hazard FMT-01 names.
#
# Everything else under docs/ - runbooks, decisions, onboarding, the index -
# is formatted normally.
docs/TP-*.md
docs/sad/
docs/trd/
docs/plan/
docs/playbook/

